## Client-facing content rules (ALWAYS apply — bake in recurring corrections)

<!-- Promote each recurring client-facing correction here so it is never re-litigated.
     End each with → pointer to its memory/feedback file. Start with the generic four;
     grow as corrections recur on THIS engagement. -->
1. **Frame risk/mitigation from the CLIENT's outcome**, never pointed at a named delivery partner. → `feedback_<slug>`
2. **No internal scaffolding on the slide face** — no transcripts, register names, raw counts, internal codes, or source-tier tags. Provenance goes in a footer / sources back-up. → `feedback_<slug>`
3. **Plain language, not insider jargon** — spell out or cut any acronym a sponsor won't know; every figure self-contained. → `feedback_<slug>`
4. **Match the host-deck template** when redrawing a slide — keep the deck's chrome. → `feedback_<slug>`

## Pointers to single-source-of-truth files

| Topic | Source-of-truth file | Use when |
|---|---|---|
| Current deliverable versions | `02_delivery/DELIVERABLES.md` | Before opening any deliverable — never grep for the newest file |
| Canonical project facts (stack, stakeholders, scope, pre-decisions) | `.claude/project-context.md` | You need a fact about the engagement |
| Comprehensive factual client reference | `02_delivery/_shared/{{CLIENT_LOWER}}_reference/_md/00_REFERENCE_SUMMARY.md` | You need the raw factual baseline — read first |
| Interpretive deltas / gaps | `02_delivery/_shared/{{CLIENT_LOWER}}_reference/_md/01_REFERENCE_INSIGHTS.md` | You need interpretation, not raw fact |
| Open-question backlog | `02_delivery/0_mobilisation/discovery_questions.md` | You need what's still owed / answered |
| Source precedence & conflict register | `02_delivery/_pm/source_precedence_and_conflict_register.md` | Two sources disagree — which one drives |
| Engagement narrative journal | `02_delivery/_pm/engagement_log.md` | You need detail behind a session/finding |

